From: Kettle Linux
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: common: line out turns on the Headphone Jack pin

The WCD codecs' MBHC reports a plug whose mic contact reads above the
headset threshold as SND_JACK_LINEOUT (MBHC_PLUG_TYPE_HIGH_HPH). The
"Headset Jack" takes that type, but its "Headphone Jack" pin only
matches SND_JACK_HEADPHONE, so the Headphone Jack control stays off,
UCM's Headphones device reads unplugged, and the sound stays on the
speakers. On the KONKR Pocket FIT Elite (WCD9395 behind its USBSS
switch) a four-pole headset reads this way at every plug: the
earpieces measure 33/35 ohms, stereo, and play once the Headphones
device is enabled. Let line out turn the Headphone Jack pin on too.
---
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/common.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/common.c
@@ -179,8 +179,12 @@
 		.mask = SND_JACK_MICROPHONE,
 	},
 	{
+		/*
+		 * Kettle: a plug MBHC reports as line out (its mic contact reads
+		 * open) is still played to through the headphone path
+		 */
 		.pin = "Headphone Jack",
-		.mask = SND_JACK_HEADPHONE,
+		.mask = SND_JACK_HEADPHONE | SND_JACK_LINEOUT,
 	},
 };
 
